content:
## Diagnosis

Two distinct defects, plus a policy violation they were hiding.

**1. "Circular dependency" — actually an evaluation-order/index error.**
`output "db_endpoint"` does `aws_db_instance.main[0].endpoint`. The resource is declared with `count`, so `main` is a *list*. When `var.envs` is empty (or when you flip to `for_each`) index `0` doesn't exist, and Terraform reports it during graph walk — which surfaces as a cycle/unknown-reference error rather than a clean "index out of range". The reference is also unnecessary: nothing else needs a fan-out here.

**2. `count` vs `for_each` type mismatch.**
`count = length(var.envs)` fans one resource set across *all* environments inside a *single state*, while every other attribute (`identifier = "${var.env}-db"`) uses the *scalar* `var.env`. Result: N identical DB identifiers → `DBInstanceAlreadyExists`, and any reordering of `var.envs` destroys/recreates databases by index. It also breaks acceptance criterion 7 (dev and prod share one state; touching prod plans changes to dev).

**Fix:** one environment per root-module invocation (workspace or `-var-file`). Delete `var.envs` entirely. If you genuinely need a fan-out over a set of names, use `for_each = toset(...)` with a *map/set key*, never `count` with a positional index.

---

## `main.tf`

```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.6"
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = "~> 5.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  region = var.region
  default_tags {
    tags = {
      Environment = var.env
      ManagedBy   = "terraform"
    }
  }
}

# Replication target for prod bucket
provider "aws" {
  alias  = "replica"
  region = var.replica_region
}

data "aws_caller_identity" "current" {}

locals {
  name    = "${var.project}-${var.env}"
  is_prod = var.env == "prod"
}
```

### RDS — the fixed resource

```hcl
resource "aws_db_subnet_group" "main" {
  name       = "${local.name}-db"
  subnet_ids = var.private_subnet_ids
}

resource "aws_security_group" "db" {
  name   = "${local.name}-db"
  vpc_id = var.vpc_id

  ingress {
    from_port       = 5432
    to_port         = 5432
    protocol        = "tcp"
    security_groups = [aws_security_group.nodes.id]
  }
}

resource "aws_kms_key" "db" {
  description             = "${local.name} RDS encryption"
  enable_key_rotation     = true
  deletion_window_in_days = 30
}

# FIX: no count / no for_each. One instance per state.
resource "aws_db_instance" "main" {
  identifier     = "${local.name}-db"
  engine         = "postgres"
  engine_version = "16.1"
  instance_class = var.db_instance_class

  allocated_storage     = var.db_allocated_storage
  max_allocated_storage = var.db_allocated_storage * 4

  db_name  = var.db_name
  username = var.db_user
  password = var.db_password # supplied via SOPS-decrypted tfvars, never committed

  db_subnet_group_name   = aws_db_subnet_group.main.name
  vpc_security_group_ids = [aws_security_group.db.id]

  # AC2 / AC1
  multi_az                = local.is_prod
  storage_encrypted       = true
  kms_key_id              = aws_kms_key.db.arn
  publicly_accessible     = false
  deletion_protection     = true
  backup_retention_period = 14
  backup_window           = "03:00-04:00"
  skip_final_snapshot     = false
  final_snapshot_identifier = "${local.name}-db-final"
  apply_immediately       = false

  lifecycle {
    prevent_destroy = true
    ignore_changes  = [password]
  }
}
```

### Outputs — the fixed reference

```hcl
# FIX: direct attribute reference, no [0] index.
output "db_endpoint" {
  value = aws_db_instance.main.endpoint
}

output "db_connection_secret_arn" {
  value = aws_secretsmanager_secret.db.arn
}

output "cluster_endpoint" {
  value = aws_eks_cluster.main.endpoint
}

output "assets_bucket" {
  value = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
}

output "cdn_domain" {
  value = aws_cloudfront_distribution.app.domain_name
}
```

### Secret (AC3)

```hcl
resource "aws_secretsmanager_secret" "db" {
  name       = "${local.name}/db-connection"
  kms_key_id = aws_kms_key.db.arn
}

resource "aws_secretsmanager_secret_version" "db" {
  secret_id = aws_secretsmanager_secret.db.id
  secret_string = jsonencode({
    host     = aws_db_instance.main.address
    port     = aws_db_instance.main.port
    dbname   = var.db_name
    username = var.db_user
    password = var.db_password
    url      = "postgresql://${var.db_user}:${urlencode(var.db_password)}@${aws_db_instance.main.endpoint}/${var.db_name}?sslmode=require"
  })
}
```

### S3 assets (AC1) — legitimate `for_each` usage, for contrast

```hcl
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "assets" {
  bucket = "${local.name}-assets-${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_versioning" "assets" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  versioning_configuration { status = "Enabled" }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration" "assets" {
  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  rule {
    apply_server_side_encryption_by_default { sse_algorithm = "AES256" }
    bucket_key_enabled = true
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block" "assets" {
  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  block_public_acls       = true
  block_public_policy     = true
  ignore_public_acls      = true
  restrict_public_buckets = true
}

# Replica bucket exists only in prod — for_each over a keyed set, not count.
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "replica" {
  for_each = local.is_prod ? toset(["replica"]) : toset([])
  provider = aws.replica
  bucket   = "${local.name}-assets-replica-${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_versioning" "replica" {
  for_each = aws_s3_bucket.replica
  provider = aws.replica
  bucket   = each.value.id
  versioning_configuration { status = "Enabled" }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket_replication_configuration" "assets" {
  for_each   = aws_s3_bucket.replica
  depends_on = [aws_s3_bucket_versioning.assets]

  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.assets.id
  role   = aws_iam_role.replication["replica"].arn

  rule {
    id     = "assets"
    status = "Enabled"
    filter {}
    delete_marker_replication { status = "Enabled" }
    destination {
      bucket        = each.value.arn
      storage_class = "STANDARD_IA"
    }
  }
}
```

> Note the pattern: `for_each = aws_s3_bucket.replica` inherits the keys of the source resource, so the dependent resources appear/disappear together with **no index arithmetic** and no cross-resource cycles.

### EKS (AC5)

```hcl
resource "aws_eks_cluster" "main" {
  name     = local.name
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.cluster.arn
  version  = "1.29"

  vpc_config {
    subnet_ids              = var.private_subnet_ids
    endpoint_public_access  = !local.is_prod
    endpoint_private_access = true
  }

  depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.cluster]
}

resource "aws_eks_node_group" "main" {
  cluster_name    = aws_eks_cluster.main.name
  node_group_name = "${local.name}-ng"
  node_role_arn   = aws_iam_role.nodes.arn
  subnet_ids      = var.private_subnet_ids
  instance_types  = [var.node_instance_type]

  scaling_config {
    desired_size = var.node_count
    min_size     = var.node_count
    max_size     = var.node_count * 2
  }
}
```

### IAM (AC4)

```hcl
data "tls_certificate" "oidc" {
  url = aws_eks_cluster.main.identity[0].oidc[0].issuer
}

resource "aws_iam_openid_connect_provider" "eks" {
  url             = aws_eks_cluster.main.identity[0].oidc[0].issuer
  client_id_list  = ["sts.amazonaws.com"]
  thumbprint_list = [data.tls_certificate.oidc.certificates[0].sha1_fingerprint]
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "app_trust" {
  statement {
    effect  = "Allow"
    actions = ["sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity"]
    principals {
      type        = "Federated"
      identifiers = [aws_iam_openid_connect_provider.eks.arn]
    }
    condition {
      test     = "StringEquals"
      variable = "${replace(aws_iam_openid_connect_provider.eks.url, "https://", "")}:sub"
      values   = ["system:serviceaccount:app:app-sa"]
    }
  }
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "app" {
  statement {
    effect    = "Allow"
    actions   = ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject", "s3:DeleteObject"]
    resources = ["${aws_s3_bucket.assets.arn}/*"]
  }
  statement {
    effect    = "Allow"
    actions   = ["secretsmanager:GetSecretValue"]
    resources = [aws_secretsmanager_secret.db.arn]
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "app" {
  name               = "${local.name}-app"
  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.app_trust.json
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "app" {
  role   = aws_iam_role.app.id
  policy = data.aws_iam_policy.app.json
}

# Dev only: programmatic IAM user. Prod uses OIDC role exclusively.
resource "aws_iam_user" "ci" {
  for_each = local.is_prod ? toset([]) : toset(["ci"])
  name     = "${local.name}-ci"
}
```

### HTTPS (AC6)

```hcl
resource "aws_lb_listener" "https" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.app.arn
  port              = 443
  protocol          = "HTTPS"
  ssl_policy        = "ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06"
  certificate_arn   = var.acm_certificate_arn

  default_action {
    type             = "forward"
    target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.app.arn
  }
}
```

---

## `variables.tf` (delta)

```hcl
variable "project"        { type = string, default = "webapp" }
variable "region"         { type = string }
variable "replica_region" { type = string, default = "us-west-2" }
variable "env" {
  type = string
  validation {
    condition     = contains(["dev", "prod"], var.env)
    error_message = "env must be dev or prod."
  }
}

# REMOVED: variable "envs" — fan-out across environments in one state
# violated environment isolation. Use -var-file or workspaces instead.

variable "db_instance_class"    { type = string }
variable "db_allocated_storage" { type = number, default = 20 }
variable "node_instance_type"   { type = string }
variable "node_count"           { type = number }
variable "acm_certificate_arn"  { type = string }
variable "vpc_id"               { type = string }
variable "private_subnet_ids"   { type = list(string) }
variable "db_name" { type = string, default = "appdb" }
variable "db_user" { type = string, default = "app_user" }
variable "db_password" {
  type      = string
  sensitive = true
  # no default — must come from SOPS-decrypted tfvars
}
```

## Environment files (AC7)

`dev.tfvars`
```hcl
env                = "dev"
region             = "us-east-1"
db_instance_class  = "db.t3.micro"
node_instance_type = "t3.medium"
node_count         = 2
```

`prod.tfvars`
```hcl
env                = "prod"
region             = "us-east-1"
db_instance_class  = "db.t3.medium"
node_instance_type = "t3.large"
node_count         = 4
```

`secrets.dev.enc.tfvars` / `secrets.prod.enc.tfvars` — SOPS+KMS encrypted, safe to commit.

Backends are separate per environment (`backend-dev.hcl` / `backend-prod.hcl` with distinct `key`), so a prod apply cannot touch dev state.

```bash
terraform init -backend-config=backend-prod.hcl -reconfigure
sops -d secrets.prod.enc.tfvars > /tmp/s.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=prod.tfvars -var-file=/tmp/s.tfvars
shred -u /tmp/s.tfvars
```

---

## Summary of changes

| # | Change | Criterion |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Removed `count = length(var.envs)`; one DB per state | fixes both errors, AC7 |
| 2 | `aws_db_instance.main[0].endpoint` → `aws_db_instance.main.endpoint` | fixes graph error |
| 3 | Deleted `var.envs` | AC7 |
| 4 | `deletion_protection = true`, `skip_final_snapshot = false`, retention 14d | AC2 |
| 5 | `storage_encrypted` + KMS, `publicly_accessible = false`, `multi_az` on prod | AC2 |
| 6 | `prevent_destroy` + `ignore_changes = [password]` | destructive-change guard |
| 7 | Bucket versioning, AES-256, full public-access block | AC1 |
| 8 | Password → Secrets Manager, sourced from SOPS tfvars | AC3 |
| 9 | Scoped IAM policies, OIDC trust, no prod IAM user | AC4 |
| 10 | Conditional resources use `for_each = toset([])`, never `count` | idiom |
